# Program data model

`src/js/config/validation-schema.js` is the single source of truth, imported by both the browser validator (`src/js/data-validator.js`) and the build-time gate (`scripts/validate-data.js`). Change the schema there — never in a copy.

## Required fields

Exactly five: `program_id`, `organization`, `program_name`, `level_of_care`, `service_domains`.

Everything else is optional, deliberately — the optional list is long and grows additively so existing records stay valid. Never promote a field to required without checking every record in `public/data/programs.json` first; `validate-data` is a blocking build step.

## Enumerations

- `service_domains`: `mental_health`, `substance_use`, `co_occurring`, `eating_disorders`
- `level_of_care`: PHP, IOP, Outpatient, Navigation, Crisis services
- Confirmation/availability enums use `yes | no | varies | unknown`. `unknown` is a real, expected value — don't treat it as falsy or as a reason to hide a program.

## Provenance gating

Some fields may only be set from a real, attributable source and must never be inferred from adjacent data: `last_verified`, `waitlist_last_confirmed`, `insurance_verified_at`, `provider_attestation_at`, `verification_tier`. Do not backfill these programmatically.

`provider_attestation_email_domain` stores a **domain only**, never a person's address. Provider free-text fields (`transportation_notes`, `discharge_friendly_notes`) hold provider-supplied text only — don't synthesize content into them.

## Two-file model

- `programs.json` — canonical records
- `programs.geocoded.json` — same records plus lat/lng, regenerated via `node scripts/geocode-programs.js` and committed

`validate-data` enforces cross-file parity: the program ID sets must match exactly, and regional snapshots under `public/data/regions/` are checked alongside them. Adding or removing a program means updating all of them together.
